component_assertion:
  method: RECIPE_TRANSCRIPTION
  completeness: COMPLETE
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: RECIPE_SOURCE
    source: https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1308
    source_record: NBRC 1308 **Trace elements solution
    supports: SUPPORT
    notes: Full table and surrounding preparation inspected. Literal thirteen-solute masses and 1 L distilled-water
      input agree; NaOH is named for the pH 6.5 step without amount, form or concentration. Final pH 7.0
      is stated after mineral addition; no second titration or additional reagent is asserted. The full
      named input set is complete relative to these sources, independently of unknown quantities and final
      volume.
  - evidence_type: RECIPE_SOURCE
    source: https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1356
    source_record: NBRC 1356 ****Trace elements solution
    supports: SUPPORT
    notes: Full table and surrounding preparation inspected. Literal thirteen-solute masses and 1 L distilled-water
      input agree; NaOH is named for the pH 6.5 step without amount, form or concentration. Final pH 7.0
      is stated after mineral addition; no second titration or additional reagent is asserted. The full
      named input set is complete relative to these sources, independently of unknown quantities and final
      volume.
  notes: 'Both complete NBRC 1308 and NBRC 1356 primary tables define this one nominal stock: the same
    13 specified solutes, 1 L distilled-water input, and NTA-first preparation, adjusted to pH 6.5 with
    NaOH before minerals are added, with final pH 7.0 stated. Recipe accession, footnote count and metadata
    encoding do not define distinct substances. Quantities are literal batch inputs, not G_PER_L concentrations:
    the sources list 1 L water, without an explicit make-up-to-final-volume instruction. NaOH amount/concentration
    are unstated. Final pH 7.0 is a stated condition, not an instruction for a second titration or evidence
    of an additional reagent. COMPLETE describes the fifteen named inputs in the complete cited preparation
    (thirteen specified solutes, distilled water and NaOH); it does not imply complete quantities, specified
    NaOH form/concentration, final volume, or final equilibrium species. Unspecified hydrate forms and
    final equilibrium species are not inferred. Occurrence context stays distinct: CultureMech:007471
    ingredients/8 (NBRC 1308; raw Trace element solution**) uses 1 ml and autoclaves the receiving mixture
    containing this stock under N2/CO2 80/20; CultureMech:007474 ingredients/6 (NBRC 1356; raw Trace element
    solution****) uses 10 ml filter-sterile stock in the separately prepared N2-handled medium. This nominal
    formulation identity does not assert identical post-processing endpoints. Case19 NBRC 1020 and 824
    occurrences remain assigned to their different reviewed NTA/KOH stock, with its separate Se/W supplement
    excluded. Raw starred labels are local occurrence provenance only, never global resolving synonyms.
    Proposal ancestry is preserved unchanged at commit d5a7613c931d45d057eaca7b5ec15280aca76c9e: A-P-NBRC1308-TRACE
    by /root/research_a and C-P-NBRC1356-TRACE by /root/research_c, with exact old payload/history/review
    bindings in successor-v2/lineage.json. This successor is authored by /root; neither old uninstalled
    identifier is installed, merged, or turned into an active alias. No source, owner or export release
    approval follows.'
